    "proposed_facts": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Independently inspected all cited canonical ranges and SET_REG_FIELD. Size 4 with shift 4 changes numerical bits 4\u20137 while preserving the low nibble; GXSetVCacheMetric uses shift 0. Old-selector resets, cached replacements, hardware destinations, selector-dependent readback and final bpSent assignment support the remaining explanation."
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "supported": true,
        "reason": "Canonical code confirms the per-routine display-list assertions, pixel-clear CHECK_GXBEGIN and command writes, unguarded local vertex-cache/XF-raster readers, GP clear register write, and distinct bpSent values. XF/raster initialization writes shared selector hardware without updating either cached GP selection. NONE and invalid-selector branches are accurately preserved. The functionality document agrees with both corrections; existing names and inherited supported knowledge are retained."
      }
    ],
    "contradictions": [
      {
        "reason": "The low-nibble baseline claim is contradicted by GP selection's size-4, shift-4 updates. Accept its supersession; the separate vertex-cache update uses bits 0\u20133.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/GXPerf.c#L291-L321"
          },
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/GXPerf.c#L624-L632"
          },
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/__gx.h#L141-L147"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "reason": "The blanket display-list prohibition overstates the local guards. Accept its supersession: pixel clear checks begin/end state instead, while vertex-cache and XF/raster readers contain no local display-list assertion. This does not assert unrestricted safety for those operations.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/GXPerf.c#L577-L703"
          },
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/__gx.h#L149-L151"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "reason": "Accept deferral of all four .data facts and its implements link. Inspected switches establish selector programming behavior, but not emitted dispatch tables, read-only status, .data attribution, table count, numerical ordering, 240-byte extent, address-entry representation or padding. These claims remain unresolved rather than disproved; no compiled-layout inference is adopted.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/extern/dolphin/src/dolphin/gx/GXPerf.c#L104-L351"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
